%% Why the concurrency fix is a lock and not a queue.
%% A stdio MCP server is one process per session. It cannot serialize on its own.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as session A<br/>own mcp process
    participant L as flock
    participant R as review repo
    participant B as session B<br/>own mcp process

    Note over A,B: NOT a shared daemon.<br/>Two sessions, two processes, one repo on disk.

    A->>L: acquire
    L-->>A: held
    A->>R: throwaway worktree A
    B->>L: acquire
    L--xB: busy — waits, does not corrupt
    A->>R: commit, push, open PR
    A->>L: release, remove worktree
    L-->>B: held
    B->>R: throwaway worktree B
    B->>R: commit, push, open PR
    B->>L: release, remove worktree

    Note over L,B: Without the lock this is the 2026-07-27 failure:<br/>branches checked out from under each other,<br/>staged files rolled into someone else's commit.
